{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:6-2","provision":"BCO 6-2","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"6-2","title":"Section 6-2","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/6-2/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/6-2","current_text":{"html":"<p>Communing members are those who have made a profession of faith in Christ, have been baptized, and have been admitted by the Session to the Lord's Table. (See <i>BCO</i> 46-4 for associate members).</p>","text":"Communing members are those who have made a profession of faith in Christ, have been baptized, and have been admitted by the Session to the Lord's Table. (See BCO 46-4 for associate members)."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"a37d71a35e8f9c0167937b7d42b075812156fb6a","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"613a69259d78b86fb70a893f9e1757ec3e9bad7c9b7578dfb01c4796d6a9b4fc","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudications.jsonl","total":11481,"expected":12405,"applied":0,"stale":11481,"unmatched":0,"unassessed":12405},"parent_id":"bco:6","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":11,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:6-2--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga40_2012__ci03.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga40_2012__ci03.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"The Procedures and Requirements for Membership in the Visible Church","year":2012,"disposition":"in conflict","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga40_2012__ci03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga40_2012__ci03.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:6-2--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga40_2012__ci03.md:occ-99d75af70d98","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga40_2012__ci03.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga40_2012__ci03.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga40_2012__ci03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"CCB found proposed overtures conflicting with BCO because the only required profession for church membership is faith in Jesus Christ, with the session judging qualifications."}},{"id":"bco:6-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga29_2001__ci04.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga29_2001__ci04.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Minimum Age for Communicant Membership","year":2001,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga29_2001__ci04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga29_2001__ci04.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:6-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga29_2001__ci04.md:occ-db953fb8169f","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga29_2001__ci04.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga29_2001__ci04.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga29_2001__ci04.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"The CCB advised that sessions must evaluate each membership request individually regardless of age, since the timing of credible faith cannot be precisely fixed."}},{"id":"bco:6-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Whether congregation may set minimum voting age for elections","year":1984,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:6-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md:occ-a96bf8b26dea","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"The BCO provides no minimum voting age for congregational meetings, except where state law imposes one for corporate votes."}},{"id":"bco:6-2--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Psiaki v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2024,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:6-2--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-dcc428aed202","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":173},"excerpt":"> Question: That the Presbytery ask the General Assembly's Permanent Committee on Judicial Business if a congregation may be permitted to set a minimum age for voting in view of BCO 6- 2, 6-4, 24-3, 25-1 and 25-3.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["minor communicant voting","congregational meeting","voting rights","good and regular standing","church bylaws","officer election","communicant membership","BCO 6-4","BCO 20-3","BCO 24-3","BCO 25-1","age restrictions","session authority"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2023-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC sustained Psiaki’s complaint and held that the CPC Session erred by ordaining and installing officers elected at a February 5, 2023 congregational meeting where the congregation’s bylaw excluded communing members under 18 from voting. Reading BCO 6-4, 25-1, and 25-7 together, the SJC ruled that all communing members are entitled to vote and that local bylaws cannot impose an age restriction; the “good and regular standing” language addresses censure, not age. The decision did not annul the completed ordination/installation, but required future elections and installations to comply with the Constitution."}},{"id":"bco:6-2--overture:ga25_1997:6","record_id":"overture:ga25_1997:6","type":"Overture","title":"Address Concern About Women Leaders in MNA Seminars","year":1997,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga25_1997.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercont